# Per-package coverage floors (ratchet: only raise, never lower).
# Baseline measured once, with Go 1.26.6, using
# `go test -coverprofile=coverage.out ./...` + coverage-gate.sh. That version is
# a historical fact about this measurement, not a pointer to the current
# toolchain pin (.tool-versions) — do not "sync" it on a Go bump; re-measure:
#   approval 76.98  checks 71.75  delivery 67.16  evidence 62.59
#   pipeline 74.23  safeio 72.67
# Floors sit below the measured baseline so the gate stays stable across Go
# patch/toolchain differences (Go 1.27 measures pipeline at 75.9 — instrumented
# statement counts differ between Go releases). The margin is NOT uniform:
# delivery 0.36pp, pipeline 0.43pp, evidence 0.69pp, approval 1.28pp — and
# deliberately wide for checks (7.15pp) and safeio (12.67pp), whose floors were
# set before their coverage grew and have not been ratcheted up since.
PKG_APPROVAL_FLOOR=75.7
PKG_CHECKS_FLOOR=64.6
PKG_DELIVERY_FLOOR=66.8
PKG_EVIDENCE_FLOOR=61.9
PKG_PIPELINE_FLOOR=73.8
PKG_SAFEIO_FLOOR=60.0
